# Purpose: Tactical boot screen / SSH MOTD. install.sh templates {{VERSION}}
#          and {{MESH_FP}} at deploy time and writes the rendered file to
#          /etc/motd. Clients SSHing into the hub see this immediately on
#          shell connect.
# Unit:    n/a (consumed by PAM via /etc/motd)
# Phase:   5 (extended in Phase 7 to surface mesh fingerprint)

   ███████╗██╗ ██████╗ ███╗   ██╗ █████╗ ██╗
   ██╔════╝██║██╔════╝ ████╗  ██║██╔══██╗██║
   ███████╗██║██║  ███╗██╔██╗ ██║███████║██║
   ╚════██║██║██║   ██║██║╚██╗██║██╔══██║██║
   ███████║██║╚██████╔╝██║ ╚████║██║  ██║███████╗
   ╚══════╝╚═╝ ╚═════╝ ╚═╝  ╚═══╝╚═╝  ╚═╝╚══════╝

   OFFLINE INFOHUB — NODE OPERATIONAL

   SSID     : SIGNAL_INFOHUB         (open, no password)
   Address  : 192.168.4.1
   Library  : http://hub.local/library/
   Ask      : http://hub.local/ask.html      (when assist + retrieve are up)
   Board    : http://hub.local/board.html
   Listen   : http://hub.local/listen.html   (when a dongle is present)
   Peers    : http://hub.local/peers.html    (when signal-mesh is up)
   Status   : http://hub.local/status.html
   API      : http://hub.local/api/status    (services block lists per-unit state)

   Mesh fingerprint : {{MESH_FP}}
   Owner token      : sudo cat /etc/signal/notes-owner-token
                      (gates DELETE /api/notes and POST /api/mesh/peers/.../trust)

   Healthcheck    : sudo /opt/signal/scripts/healthcheck.sh
   Factory reset  : sudo /opt/signal/scripts/factory_reset.sh --yes

   No internet egress  ·  MIT licensed  ·  {{VERSION}}

